From cbe2e009c2cf024df5b93bce311079744418121c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:31:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] assurance: metered API keys, Stripe billing, fly.io
 deployment

WHY
  The Art. 14 register has no way to take money. Endpoints are open or
  gated by a shared static key. Nothing distinguishes a prospect from a
  customer, and nothing stops a prospect using the whole product free.

WHAT
  - src/assurance/billing/plans.py      entitlements declared in code
  - src/assurance/billing/accounts.py   accounts, hashed API keys, UTC-day quota
  - src/assurance/billing/stripe_gateway.py  checkout, portal, webhook HMAC
  - src/assurance/api/billing_routes.py /v1/plans /v1/checkout /v1/me /v1/billing/*
  - src/assurance/api/deps.py           principal, entitlement (402), quota (429)
  - src/assurance/api/routes.py         free tier: /v1/spec/fields, /v1/spec/validate
  - deploy/assurance/                   Dockerfile, fly.toml, README

CUSTOMER VALUE
  A buyer can self-serve from the free validator to a paid register in one
  flow, with no call and no invoice cycle. The free validator catches real
  submission errors (absent awareness timestamp, non-EU Member State codes,
  over-length fields) before ENISA rejects them.

RISK
  Stripe keys absent -> /v1/checkout returns 503 naming the missing variable;
  no other route is affected. Webhook forgery is refused by HMAC-SHA256 with
  a 300s replay window. API keys are stored only as sha256; shown once.

ROLLBACK
  git revert this commit. Patch 001/002 surfaces are untouched apart from
  deps.py, whose prior static-key behaviour is superseded, not extended.

TESTS
  245 passed (32 new in tests/test_assurance_billing.py), ruff clean.

SUCCESS CONDITION
  One paid checkout completed end to end against a live deployment.

